WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Archaeologists have dated the world's oldest known shipwreck to 2,700 BC from pottery cargo found off Turkey. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 217. Associate Professor Hakkan Oniz of Actoniz University led the recovery from shallow waters near Kecova on the southern Turkish coast, according to Fizz.org. The cargo included large, ovoid amphorae with two handles and raised horizontal clay belts around their widest parts. Some of those vessels still carry residues

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.700
from eastern Mediterranean production regions. The ship appears to have sought shelter during

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.980
a storm before striking rocks. Its timbers then disappeared while the ceramic state embedded

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.000
in the rocky underwater slope. Pottery shapes and manufacturing techniques supplied the

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.580
primary dating evidence, spanning 2,700 to 2,400 BC. That age predates the previous record

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:58.740
holder, a wreck-off docos in Greece about 4,200 years ago, by roughly 300 years.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.800
Divers spent four months extracting the vessels while working around barnacles on the slope.

00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:09.675
Manufacturing details on the Kikovah jars still point towards specific eastern Mediterranean

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:10.675
production regions.

00:01:11.235 --> 00:01:15.775
The vessel's coastal path lines up with early Bronze Age exchange that moved cedar,

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:19.415
metals, and resins toward Egypt and neighboring societies.

00:01:19.415 --> 00:01:24.115
Those roots also tied the Levant into the same networks during the Pyramid Age.

00:01:24.595 --> 00:01:28.855
Continued excavation is aimed at showing how often such voyages actually ran.

00:01:29.475 --> 00:01:33.775
Durable ceramics are reconstructing those maritime connections, even though the wooden hall

00:01:33.775 --> 00:01:34.275
is gone.

00:01:35.323 --> 00:01:39.963
Northeastern University researchers mapped neural circuits in the roundworm C elegans

00:01:39.963 --> 00:01:45.203
to compare how males and hermaphrodites process sensory input, according to Fizz.org.

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:50.623
work. The entire nervous system of this worm consists of exactly 302 neurons whose connections

00:01:50.623 --> 00:01:56.183
have already been fully charted. The comparison used that complete connectome to set male circuits

00:01:56.183 --> 00:02:01.543
beside her maferdite circuits directly. Distinct wiring patterns appeared in sensory regions

00:02:01.543 --> 00:02:07.743
tied to mate detection and environmental navigation. Experiments exposed each sex variant to identical

00:02:07.743 --> 00:02:13.743
stimuli and recorded divergent response patterns in those sensory processing circuits. Compact

00:02:13.743 --> 00:02:17.443
nervous systems produce sex-specific information handling without large

00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:22.166
differences in neuron count. University of Edinburgh researchers followed the

00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:27.566
Lothian Birth cohort in 1936 and collected cognitive scores from 866

00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:33.106
participants between ages 70 and 82. The test covered memory, processing speed

00:02:33.106 --> 00:02:37.806
and spatial understanding according to science daily. Post-mortem brain tissue

00:02:37.806 --> 00:02:42.306
from people with faster decline contained fewer large nerve fibers. The same

00:02:42.306 --> 00:02:47.566
tissue showed an abnormal buildup of unhealthy myelin around remaining fibers. Lower levels

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:53.606
of the protective protein NRF2 inside oligodendrocytes correlated with both the myelin excess and

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:59.786
the fiber loss. When researchers experimentally lowered NRF2 in mouse oligodendrocytes, the

00:02:59.786 --> 00:03:04.486
animals developed the same myelin overproduction and large fiber reduction seen in the human

00:03:04.486 --> 00:03:11.975
samples. The NRF2 pathway is already targeted by an approved multiple sclerosis drug, a 24-year

00:03:11.975 --> 00:03:17.355
monitoring program across multiple forest sites recorded an average 3% annual rise in

00:03:17.355 --> 00:03:20.595
methane uptake under rising temperatures and declining rainfall.

00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:25.875
Science Daily describes researchers tracking gas fluxes at the soil surface and linking

00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:30.675
the upward trend to microbial communities that oxidize atmospheric methane more effectively

00:03:30.675 --> 00:03:31.715
as soils dry.

00:03:32.435 --> 00:03:37.135
The result runs counter to earlier models that predicted reduced methane removal from warming

00:03:37.135 --> 00:03:37.615
soils.

00:03:37.615 --> 00:03:43.595
Methane-consuming bacteria appear to gain advantage under the dryer, warmer regimes now observed

00:03:43.595 --> 00:03:45.455
in many temperate and boreal forests.

00:03:46.473 --> 00:03:51.213
Most people assume warming forest ground will pour extra methane into the air as the climate

00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:51.733
heats up.

00:03:52.333 --> 00:03:53.753
The soil is doing something else.

00:03:54.273 --> 00:03:59.153
Methane first diffuses into pore spaces where specialized microbes take it as an energy

00:03:59.153 --> 00:03:59.533
source.

00:04:00.033 --> 00:04:03.333
Those microbes convert the gas into carbon dioxide and water.

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:08.453
When soil moisture drops, the same bacteria can process larger volumes of atmospheric

00:04:08.453 --> 00:04:10.773
methane that would otherwise remain in the air.

00:04:11.313 --> 00:04:14.633
Forests already cover roughly 30% of Earth's land surface.

00:04:15.173 --> 00:04:19.653
Even modest per-area increases in methane removal could influence global atmospheric

00:04:19.653 --> 00:04:20.873
budgets over decades.

00:04:21.453 --> 00:04:25.893
The record is one of the longest continuous soil gas series available for testing climate

00:04:25.893 --> 00:04:29.393
models that had assumed net methane release from warming ground.

00:04:29.393 --> 00:04:35.553
Additional measurements at sites with different tree species and soil types will show how broadly the pattern applies.

00:04:36.133 --> 00:04:43.333
Forest management that preserves soil structure and microbial diversity is being discussed as one way to keep that microbial work intact.

00:04:43.993 --> 00:04:51.133
Future work could examine whether similar uptake increases occur in agricultural or grassland soils under comparable climate shifts.

00:04:51.753 --> 00:04:58.833
Long-term environmental monitoring networks are what make these slow soil changes visible at all, because shorter experiments miss them.

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:04.643
Researchers at Yuliege and Humboldt University isolated individual visual pigments from

00:05:04.643 --> 00:05:09.003
mantis shrimp eyes and measured their responses to red wavelengths that few other animals

00:05:09.003 --> 00:05:09.563
can detect.

00:05:10.103 --> 00:05:16.203
The study published in science advances examined roughly 30 visual pigments in total, far exceeding

00:05:16.203 --> 00:05:17.403
the three found in humans.

00:05:17.903 --> 00:05:21.643
Certain pigments returned to their original state after red light exposure ended.

00:05:22.323 --> 00:05:27.323
Direct spectroscopy on purified proteins, not mixtures, confirmed that reversible switching.

00:05:27.323 --> 00:05:32.323
The reversible property emerged only after the team analyzed each pigment separately.

00:05:32.923 --> 00:05:37.203
Fizz.org notes that this light-controlled behavior is being considered as a path toward

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.703
new optogenetic tools.

00:05:39.761 --> 00:05:44.121
Cornell researchers applied voltage to slide layers within ultra-thin graphing sheets

00:05:44.121 --> 00:05:48.381
and watched magnetic states switch and then stay switched after the voltage came off.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:53.761
Fizz.org reports that the transitions arise from altered interlayer coupling that modifies

00:05:53.761 --> 00:05:56.441
electron interactions within the two-dimensional lattice.

00:05:56.441 --> 00:06:01.401
Transport measurements and spectroscopic measurements both confirm the magnetic changes

00:06:01.401 --> 00:06:03.221
without continuous external input.

00:06:03.761 --> 00:06:07.461
Once set, those quantum properties in the layered material remain stable.

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:12.081
Mechanical positioning of the layers is the lever that stores the magnetic information.

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:18.520
The National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, used the James Webb Space Telescope

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.140
to observe a turbulent world 20 light years away.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:29.100
The telescope identified three repeating atmospheric states shaped by temperature shifts and cloud redistribution, according to Science Daily.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:34.940
Repeated observations revealed an unexpectedly orderly pattern despite the planet's overall turbulence.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:41.060
Specific temperature changes consistently triggered measurable movements and cloud cover that defined each state.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:48.160
The data set supplies a concrete template for modeling weather dynamics on other distant planets where direct measurements remain limited.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:53.180
Further telescope time on similar targets could test whether the three-state cycle appears

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:53.940
more widely.

00:06:54.882 --> 00:06:59.622
A worldwide trust survey connected poor access to healthcare and unequal distribution of

00:06:59.622 --> 00:07:05.162
research benefits with measurably lower public confidence in science, according to Fizz.org.

00:07:06.042 --> 00:07:10.322
Respondents in regions where local communities hold limited influence over research priorities

00:07:10.322 --> 00:07:11.982
reported the widest trust gaps.

00:07:12.662 --> 00:07:17.442
Perceptions of fairness in who gains from scientific advances shaped overall attitudes toward

00:07:17.442 --> 00:07:22.742
the Enterprise. Experts suggest that improving access and participation could narrow those gaps

00:07:22.742 --> 00:07:27.642
without requiring changes to the underlying research itself. The survey covered multiple

00:07:27.642 --> 00:07:34.094
continents and found consistent patterns across differing economic contexts. Michigan State University

00:07:34.094 --> 00:07:40.294
researchers applied natural language processing to more than 38,000 popular songs and documented

00:07:40.294 --> 00:07:46.254
a gradual decline in direct references to emotions and relationships. The downward trend appeared both

00:07:46.254 --> 00:07:51.114
across successive generations of artists, and within the careers of individual performers,

00:07:51.374 --> 00:07:56.554
according to Fizz.org, quantification of emotional language showed the shift occurred steadily

00:07:56.554 --> 00:07:59.134
rather than in abrupt jumps tied to single events.

00:07:59.794 --> 00:08:04.794
The pattern tracks evolving cultural norms around how popular music conveys personal experience.

00:08:05.434 --> 00:08:10.294
Further analysis could test whether the same trajectory holds in non-English language music

00:08:10.294 --> 00:08:10.714
markets.

00:08:10.714 --> 00:08:16.211
all-Flandegrand developed a technique for distinguishing between different gene variants during

00:08:16.211 --> 00:08:22.051
his postdoctoral work at Caltech in the 1980s. That invention generated patents and directly

00:08:22.051 --> 00:08:27.591
ceded a series of companies focused on genetic analysis tools, according to life science focus.

00:08:28.291 --> 00:08:33.171
Subsequent innovations and detection methods built on the original approach for identifying genetic

00:08:33.171 --> 00:08:38.591
differences at scale. The foundational technique continues to underpin diagnostic and research

00:08:38.591 --> 00:08:41.191
applications still in routine laboratory use.

00:08:41.771 --> 00:08:46.671
Landegren has described how many later projects trace their conceptual roots to that early gene

00:08:46.671 --> 00:08:47.491
variant work.

00:08:47.971 --> 00:08:53.031
Over the past seven days, mapping kept turning up, from every cell division in a mammalian

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:56.171
embryo to snake bite cases missing from official tallies.

00:08:57.076 --> 00:09:01.896
Genome editing maps now follow development from early embryo through organ formation and

00:09:01.896 --> 00:09:03.736
set a new benchmark for those studies.

00:09:04.616 --> 00:09:08.916
Expanded snake bite counts showed official records still miss a large share of cases and

00:09:08.916 --> 00:09:14.316
prompted calls for better surveillance. A 47-year fitness study found that measurable declines

00:09:14.316 --> 00:09:21.125
and strength began around age 35, even among people who keep exercising. Before we go, continued

00:09:21.125 --> 00:09:26.105
residue analysis of the Kekova pottery is meant to clarify which ports supplied the cargo.

